{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Ascendancy and The End of Heartache combine aggression with memorable melody, which makes them natural next choices after my In Flames and Soilwork listening.",
    "The War Within fits the riff-driven intensity I enjoy in Advance And Vanquish, while Hypnotize appeals to my interest in unusual rhythms and heavy hooks reflected in Tool and Disturbed."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "None of these albums felt clearly wrong for me; leaving some unchosen reflects what I want today rather than dislike.",
    "Animosity, Lost and Found, and the Sevendust albums fit my broader taste, but their heavy grooves interest me less right now than the melodic metal choices."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Shared heaviness seems to carry too much weight: aggression alone does not explain why Ascendancy and The End of Heartache stand out to me.",
    "The list treats several branches of my heavy listening as equally immediate interests, although I would only choose a few albums on this visit."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The balance between harsh vocals, melodic hooks, and aggressive riffs matters more to my choices today than heaviness by itself.",
    "An album can suit my taste without being a current priority; The Oncoming Storm and Vol. 3 interest me enough to save for later."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understand my taste for heavy music, but could better distinguish my current preference for melodic aggression from albums I would explore later."
}"}
